  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-483-proof is always GraalVM's own `UnsupportedFeatureError` — never the library's
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-484-error type, message, or stack frames. Some libraries catch that error and
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-485-re-throw their own without setting a cause, which destroys the evidence a
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-486-cause walk needs; recognising such a library-specific signature to tolerate
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:487:the failure anyway is the §FS-test-contract.4.2 violation, not a workaround
