  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-482-Tolerating requires positive proof that Native Image refused an operation. The
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-483-proof is always GraalVM's own `UnsupportedFeatureError` — never the library's
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-484-error type, message, or stack frames. Some libraries catch that error and
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-485-re-throw their own without setting a cause, which destroys the evidence a
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-486-cause walk needs; recognising such a library-specific signature to tolerate
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:487:the failure anyway is the §FS-test-contract.4.2 violation, not a workaround
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-488-for it.
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-489-
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-490-`NativeImageSupport.runToleratingUnsupportedFeature` from
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-491-`org.graalvm.internal.tck` is the one sanctioned way to apply the exception. It
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-492-runs the action and accepts a failure only on proof, in this order:
  --
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-500-
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-501-Printed throwables are inspected as objects, never matched as text, so unrelated
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-502-output naming the error cannot buy tolerance. An `AssertionError` or
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-503-`VirtualMachineError` is always re-thrown, so a genuine assertion failure after a
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-504-tolerated one is never masked. Anything else is re-thrown unchanged. On the JVM the action runs and asserts
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:505:normally, so the helper is never a skip (§FS-test-contract.4.1).
  docs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-506-
