functional-spec/test-contract.md-491-`org.graalvm.internal.tck` is the one sanctioned way to apply the exception. It\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-492-runs the action and accepts a failure only on proof, in this order:\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-500-\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-501-Printed throwables are inspected as objects, never matched as text, so unrelated\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-502-output naming the error cannot buy tolerance. An `AssertionError` or\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-503-`VirtualMachineError` is always re-thrown, so a genuine assertion failure after a\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-504-tolerated one is never masked. Anything else is re-thrown unchanged. On the JVM the action runs and asserts\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:505:normally, so the helper is never a skip (§FS-test-contract.4.1).\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-506-\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-507-```java\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-508-NativeImageSupport.runToleratingUnsupportedFeature(() -> {\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-509-    Plugin plugin = PluginLoader.load(pluginJar, \"example.Plugin\");\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-510-    assertThat(plugin.name()).isEqualTo(\"example\");\n--\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-554-self-attach, class redefinition, instrumentation, native-image substitutions,\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-555-URL/plugin/OSGi class loader paths, custom class loaders that introduce classes\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-556-not already in the image, or classes that exist only through a custom class\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-557-loader. This includes Byte Buddy-backed inline mocking, static mocking,\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md-558-construction mocking, and concrete-class mocking. Prefer statically\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:559:representable behavior (§FS-test-contract.3.2).\ndocs/functio